      ":question/id": "b91051bc-fde1-529a-86ef-58ee2547700f",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}a-c &=11b \\\\ 13c-6a &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $a,b,c$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1a-11b-1c &=0 \\\\ -6a+0b+13c &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -11 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -11 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 13 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
